## Re-syncing with upstream

This repository shares history with qm, so upstream syncs are ordinary merges:

    git remote add qm https://github.com/divyajotsingh093/qm
    git fetch qm main
    git merge qm/main

The inherited `update-qm` skill automates this and opens a sync PR. The
`upstream-pr` skill sends a change the other way, for fixes that belong in qm
core rather than here.

## Known gaps in this environment

`plugins/web-ui` cannot be installed from behind a restricted egress proxy. Its
dependency `@earendil-works/pi-web-ui` requires `xlsx` pinned to a direct
tarball at `cdn.sheetjs.com` rather than the npm registry, which returns 403
under a default-deny policy.

This is an egress restriction, not a defect: CI installs, typechecks, tests,
builds and boots the web-ui production image successfully. Only local work
behind such a proxy is affected, and only for that one plugin — admin, portal
and auth install from the registry and pass locally (77, 105 and 52 tests).

A dependency fetched from a vendor CDN rather than the registry is still worth
removing on its own merits.
